A||||3||Rrazzz||Tire Pressure for 88 GT?||||5||
Z||000000||Rrazzz||06-28-2000||06:02 PM||||Can someone please check the door sticker on their 1988 GT or Formula and tell me what GM's recommended tire pressure was for the 205/60-15 front and 215/60-15 rear tire combination. <P>The previous owner replaced the original 14" wheels with 7x15 wheels on my 88 coupe. I'm currently using Pirelli SuperTouring P4000 P205 and 215/60HR-15 (44 psi max). I've checked the Helm's Service Manual. But it's inconsistent, indicating 30 psi front and 35 psi rear on page 3E-10 and 30psi front and rear on page 0B-8.<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>Rrazzz||||reg||5
Z||000001||gixxer||06-28-2000||07:17 PM||||The door sticker (88 Formula) sez 30 PSI for both front (205/60-15) and rear (215/60-15).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-29-2000||02:13 AM||||The tire pressure on the door was for the original tires. Tire pressure varies between tires. Go by what is on the tire not the door. The Pirelli's you have are 44psi max so you should have them at about 38 psi.<BR>Going down to 30 psi will affect handling and wear.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rrazzz||06-29-2000||06:27 PM||||Thanks. I will experiment with pressures in the 30's, keep the front and rear about the same.||||reg||7
